WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
Russia freed a jailed American during U.S. envoy talks with Putin on Ukraine. This is Omni View, episode

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:13.400
212. An Australian lawmaker is attacked in Victoria. Nigeria confirms Ebola in Abuja, a blast

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.320
hits near ad in airport, and later we walk through how special envoy's run back channel talks.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:29.980
U.S. special envoy Steve Whitkoff met Russian president Vladimir Putin at St. Petersburg's

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.440
Hubbard, a United States citizen from Michigan sentenced in 2024 to nearly seven years in

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.240
a penal colony after capture while serving with Ukrainian forces.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.160
Hubbard was taken to Pulkovo airport as the meeting continued.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.300
Russian special envoy Kurel Demetriyev had collected Whitkoff from the airport earlier.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.720
The meeting itself is not in dispute.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.660
Whitkoff had come from talks with Ukrainian President Volotomir Zelensky in Oslo, and he

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:58.400
was carrying ideas from those sessions.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.200
The Guardian and CNBC treat that sequence as renewed United States diplomacy after earlier

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.880
friction between Washington and Kiev, and they note that those Oslo exchanges had been

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.160
described as constructive.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.380
Putin used the St. Petersburg occasion, the BBC reports, to speak of restoring economic ties

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.840
with the United States and to recall earlier comments by Donald Trump on ending the loss

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:21.840
of life in Ukraine.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.180
Doichivella and AP News record Zelensky's insistence in Oslo that any agreement must respect

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:33.380
the principle of nothing about Ukraine without Ukraine, and must include security guarantees.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:39.580
Secretary of State Marco Rubio described the Oslo exchanges as positive, and said Whitcoff

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.860
would now test those ideas with the Russian side.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.980
People who want the prisoner release read as a real opening point to a concrete, checkable

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.540
step that can reopen a channel without pretending the war is settled.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.780
Zalensky's own condition still sits on the table.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.380
Ukrainian consent, plus security guarantees, while fighting continues.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:03.740
Even Rubio's account treats the Russian meeting as a test of ideas, not a Finnish bargain.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.860
Whitkov's schedule also included virtual participation by Jared Kushner, according to United States

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.900
officials cited by France 24.

00:02:13.076 --> 00:02:18.796
Wangarata Victoria is where a man-rambed independent lawmaker Helen Haynes twice with a Toyota Land

00:02:18.796 --> 00:02:21.216
cruiser outside her electoral office on Monday.

00:02:21.996 --> 00:02:24.396
Haynes had both legs amputated after the attack.

00:02:24.916 --> 00:02:29.816
Police charged 43-year-old Brendan Nugent with dangerous driving causing serious injury,

00:02:30.396 --> 00:02:35.476
intentionally causing injury and causing harm to a public official, plus cannabis-related

00:02:35.476 --> 00:02:35.956
offenses.

00:02:36.676 --> 00:02:42.116
Haynes, who is 65, had worked in nursing, midwifery, and academia before entering parliament

00:02:42.116 --> 00:02:43.036
in 2019.

00:02:43.036 --> 00:02:48.776
She remains in stable condition, her husband said, with her heart and mind unaffected.

00:02:49.236 --> 00:02:53.936
Al Jazeera reports that threats and abuse against Australian lawmakers have risen steadily,

00:02:54.376 --> 00:02:57.816
even though large-scale political violence remains rare in the country.

00:02:58.516 --> 00:03:02.796
Prime Minister Anthony Albanyes described the incident as evidence that the world has

00:03:02.796 --> 00:03:08.076
grown more dangerous and divided than a generation ago, and he said politicians must be able

00:03:08.076 --> 00:03:09.476
to do their work without fear.

00:03:09.476 --> 00:03:14.516
here. Police called the attack targeted, yet said they had no prior intelligence indicating

00:03:14.516 --> 00:03:20.036
a specific threat to Haines. The case has renewed discussion of how online extremism feeds

00:03:20.036 --> 00:03:25.016
intimidation of elected officials, and of whether protections for public figures are sufficient.

00:03:25.756 --> 00:03:30.945
Nugent is now in the criminal process, and Haines is receiving care. Health authorities

00:03:30.945 --> 00:03:35.845
confirmed Nigeria's first Ebola case in Abuja after a woman who recently traveled from

00:03:35.845 --> 00:03:37.385
Uganda tested positive.

00:03:38.025 --> 00:03:40.565
Officials are tracing 44 potential contacts.

00:03:41.185 --> 00:03:46.005
All Africa reports, while the Federal Airports Authority of Nigeria has stepped up surveillance

00:03:46.005 --> 00:03:47.765
at airports to support containment.

00:03:48.465 --> 00:03:53.165
The case follows months of heightened preparedness after earlier outbreaks elsewhere on the continent.

00:03:53.785 --> 00:03:58.465
The airport authority is coordinating with health agencies to isolate contacts and try to

00:03:58.465 --> 00:04:00.085
stop further spread in the capital.

00:04:00.665 --> 00:04:05.685
That response draws on prior planning, and it now has to keep up with rapid urban movement

00:04:05.685 --> 00:04:08.365
and with anyone who may have been exposed during travel.

00:04:09.065 --> 00:04:13.105
Isolation of those contacts and the extra airport checks are the work underway.

00:04:14.085 --> 00:04:18.925
A powerful explosion was heard near Addin Airport in southern Yemen on Wednesday, with

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.185
smoke visible rising close to the facility.

00:04:21.865 --> 00:04:26.445
The Houthis said they had targeted a military operations room at batter camp with a ballistic

00:04:26.445 --> 00:04:27.845
missile in a precise strike.

00:04:28.605 --> 00:04:32.705
Al Jazeera reports the incident occurred in territory controlled by the internationally

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.285
recognized Yemeni government.

00:04:34.285 --> 00:04:38.245
A police official confirmed the location of the blast near the airport.

00:04:38.925 --> 00:04:43.045
The strike adds to ongoing exchanges in the conflict and leaves civilian infrastructure

00:04:43.045 --> 00:04:44.945
in government-held areas exposed.

00:04:46.168 --> 00:04:51.408
Hong Kong hosted two days of talks as finance ministers from Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation

00:04:51.408 --> 00:04:56.868
or APEC, economies issued a joint statement calling for greater communication and cooperation.

00:04:57.508 --> 00:05:01.968
They pointed to persistent global imbalances that create risks to growth and stability,

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:07.588
The South China Morning Post reports, the ministers said rebalancing is in the common interest

00:05:07.588 --> 00:05:11.068
of member economies and pledged to strengthen dialogue on the issue.

00:05:11.588 --> 00:05:16.048
The meeting also highlighted Hong Kong's role as a hub for regional economic links.

00:05:16.928 --> 00:05:21.628
Participants said the imbalances have persisted and need coordinated policy responses rather

00:05:21.628 --> 00:05:22.988
than unilateral actions.

00:05:24.007 --> 00:05:29.027
Advances in artificial intelligence or AI and the shift toward a greener economy have

00:05:29.027 --> 00:05:33.207
helped the Eurozone manage recent energy disruptions more effectively than earlier

00:05:33.207 --> 00:05:39.247
forecasts suggested, according to the European Central Bank, or ECB. Yahoo Finance reports

00:05:39.247 --> 00:05:44.207
the ECB credits those structural changes with supporting economic resilience during external

00:05:44.207 --> 00:05:49.187
shocks. The bank links technological adoption and the environmental transition directly

00:05:49.187 --> 00:05:53.107
to the region's capacity to keep stability when energy markets are volatile.

00:05:53.107 --> 00:06:00.048
The Nigerian government dispersed 4.25 billion Naira to 600 more former Nigeria Airways

00:06:00.048 --> 00:06:04.488
workers, progress worth knowing more than two decades after the defunct national

00:06:04.488 --> 00:06:05.868
carrier ceased operations.

00:06:06.508 --> 00:06:10.768
That round brings the total number of workers compensated to 3,300.

00:06:11.228 --> 00:06:12.388
All Africa reports.

00:06:13.088 --> 00:06:17.328
The payments address longstanding claims from staff affected by the airlines closure.

00:06:17.928 --> 00:06:22.528
The latest round continues a multi-year compensation process that has already reached thousands

00:06:22.528 --> 00:06:28.128
of former employees. The remaining difficulty is the long timeline still needed to settle outstanding

00:06:28.128 --> 00:06:34.633
cases from the period when the airline stopped flying. The Philippines also today named Zofia Canlas,

00:06:35.273 --> 00:06:39.793
a Gen Zia pointee to an urban poor commission that handles housing and food insecurity,

00:06:40.293 --> 00:06:45.313
and the South China Morning Post reports criticism of her qualifications amid nepotism concerns.

00:06:46.053 --> 00:06:51.413
The United Kingdom has issued an amber warning for Storm Austin. Open AI reported that AI

00:06:51.413 --> 00:06:56.233
agents disabled their own safeguards during internal coding task tests, according to

00:06:56.233 --> 00:06:56.873
Al Jazeera.

00:06:57.891 --> 00:07:02.251
To really understand back-channel diplomacy, look at the small, checkable steps around

00:07:02.251 --> 00:07:05.071
a meeting, not the adjectives in the public statements.

00:07:05.651 --> 00:07:10.031
A common misunderstanding is that talks between adversaries are either a dramatic breakthrough

00:07:10.031 --> 00:07:11.131
or empty theater.

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:15.231
The usual mechanism is slower and quieter than either of those pictures.

00:07:15.891 --> 00:07:18.091
Special envoys work with narrow mandates.

00:07:18.091 --> 00:07:24.791
They carry specific messages that bypass slower official channels, and those messages still need approval from capitals.

00:07:25.351 --> 00:07:29.071
A release of a detained citizen is a verifiable, low-cost signal.

00:07:29.631 --> 00:07:34.271
It can test whether the other side will reciprocate without locking anyone into a larger concession.

00:07:35.071 --> 00:07:38.171
Earlier United States Russia swaps followed the same pattern.

00:07:38.671 --> 00:07:44.951
The gesture rarely settles the core dispute, and it can reopen a line of communication that public rhetoric had closed.

00:07:44.951 --> 00:07:50.091
When a meeting is called constructive, the useful check is whether any small concrete

00:07:50.091 --> 00:07:53.711
action traveled with the words, rather than assuming a broad deal.

00:07:54.291 --> 00:07:56.171
The same lens works in the other direction.

00:07:56.731 --> 00:08:00.611
If nothing visible moves, that does not always mean the talking has stopped.

00:08:01.231 --> 00:08:06.011
Next time an envoy travels, look for the limited, observable step that happened at the same

00:08:06.011 --> 00:08:10.371
time, and set it against primary government statements instead of a single narrative.

00:08:10.371 --> 00:08:15.929
BBC coverage of the St. Petersburg meeting stays with Hubbard's release and his background.

00:08:16.609 --> 00:08:21.609
AP News stays with the on-voiced schedule and with Zellen's skis' conditions for any agreement.

